# Scoped Deploy + Hosting Preflight

When the user asks to deploy, choose the smallest deploy target that matches the change.

## Default deploy strategy

- Frontend/UI-only changes: run `npm run build:check` first, then deploy hosting only.
- Function-only changes: deploy only changed functions.
- Firestore rules/index changes: deploy only firestore.
- Use full `firebase deploy` only when multiple deploy targets changed, or when the user explicitly asks for full deploy.

## Commands

- Hosting only: `firebase deploy --only hosting`
- One function: `firebase deploy --only functions:<functionName>`
- Multiple functions: `firebase deploy --only functions:a,functions:b`
- Firestore only: `firebase deploy --only firestore`

## Communication requirement

Before running deploy, state in one short sentence what target is being deployed and why that scope was chosen.

If the deploy enables new always-on Functions, schedulers, or wide listener changes, also run the **Cost check** block from [`cost-estimate-before-action.mdc`](./cost-estimate-before-action.mdc) and get CEO approval first.
